      m_Calls: []
  m_text: '<size=140%><b>Credits and sources</b></size>


    <b><color=#F2C38B>Opportunity</color></b>

    A game made for the NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026.


    <b><color=#F2C38B>Mission facts</color></b>

    Landing on 25 January 2004 in Eagle crater, Meridiani Planum. Designed to last 90 sols (Martian days); worked for almost 15 years and drove more than 45 km. Last contact on 10 June 2018. NASA declared the end of the mission on 13 February 2019. Final resting spot: Perseverance Valley.

    <size=80%><link="https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mer-opportunity/"><u>https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mer-opportunity/</u></link></size>


    <b><color=#F2C38B>Dust storm and distance record</color></b>

    The planet-wide dust storm of June 2018, and Opportunity''s distance record on another world, which held until 11 October 2026.

    <size=80%><link="https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mars-exploration-rovers-spirit-and-opportunity/"><u>https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mars-exploration-rovers-spirit-and-opportunity/</u></link></size>


    <b><color=#F2C38B>Blueberries and water</color></b>

    The "blueberries" are small spheres of hematite, a mineral that typically forms in water.

    <size=80%><link="https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mars-exploration-rovers-spirit-and-opportunity/science-highlights/"><u>https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mars-exploration-rovers-spirit-and-opportunity/science-highlights/</u></link></size>


    <b><color=#F2C38B>Images</color></b>

    Blueberries photo: PLACEHOLDER. Replace with the real NASA image, its PIA number and credit line from the JPL Photojournal.


    <b><color=#F2C38B>3D model</color></b>

    Mars Exploration Rover model: NASA Visualization Technology Applications and Development (VTAD). NASA 3D Resources are free to download and use; see the NASA Images and Media Usage Guidelines.

    <size=80%><link="https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/"><u>https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/</u></link></size>


    <b><color=#F2C38B>Software</color></b>

    Made with Unity. Rover model imported with glTFast (Apache License 2.0). Text in Liberation Sans (SIL Open Font License).'
